      "writtenOn": "2024-02-29T20:07:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dropping an idea here.\n\nWhat about extending `GattService` ?\n\nThis way you don\u0027t have to change anything in `ScanManager` as the Service it has is always matching\n\nSee this code example:\n\n```java\nclass Foo {\n  String getName() { return \"Foo\"; }\n  String getFoo() { return \"Foo\"; }\n\n}\n\nclass Bar extends Foo {\n  String getName() { return \"Bar\"; }\n}\n\nFoo foo \u003d new Foo();\nSystem.out.println(\"Hello, \" + foo.getName());\n\nFoo bar \u003d new Bar();\nSystem.out.println(\"Hello, \" + bar.getName() + \" -- \" + bar.getFoo());\n```\n\nBar can be interpreted as a Foo, Aka the scanManagerService could be downcaat as a GattService.\n\n\nObviously, this only work as long as there is no new method in scanManagerService that are called from external. In this case, an explicit cast to `scanManagerService` is necessary",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "13e06e21f7fdb654077ed1255d580780687959ca",
